# Line endings. Deliberately surgical rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto`, so
# adding this file does not renormalise everything. Shell scripts must reach the
# Linux bundle with LF: a CRLF latticegen2.sh fails with "bad interpreter", and
# the archive is built on a Windows checkout where autocrlf would otherwise
# apply.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf

# OCCT .brep test fixtures are byte-exact geometry captured from a real failed
# run (test/invalid-vertex-tolerance-*.brep). They are ASCII, so autocrlf would
# happily rewrite their line endings on checkout; pinning them as binary keeps
# every platform reading the same bytes the measurements were taken on.
*.brep  -text

# Files excluded from `git archive`, and therefore from the release bundles that
# tools/build_release.py assembles from it. Keeping the payload to tracked files
# only is what guarantees a stray working-tree directory can never reach a
# published asset.
#
# Rationale per entry:
#   .claude/          local agent state, including a full duplicate checkout
#   .github/          CI definitions, of no use to an end user
#   CLAUDE.md         instructions for the coding agent, not for the operator
#   docs/usernotes.md private working notes
#   docs/release.md   the developer's release manual (docs/release.md itself)
#   test/             59 MB of fixtures and golden samples; verification runs in
#                     CI only (docs/specification.md §6.3)
#   tools/            dev harnesses and the release builder

/.claude            export-ignore
/.github            export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md          export-ignore
/docs/usernotes.md  export-ignore
/docs/release.md    export-ignore
/test               export-ignore
/tools              export-ignore
